# Battle Core Mechanics

## Core Principles
- Iterative development approach
- Clear separation of battle phases
- Maintain simplicity in battle system changes
- Focus on core functionality first

## Development Guidelines
1. State Management
   - Single source of truth for battalion states
   - Direct state updates without nesting
   - Clear state transitions
   - Atomic operations

2. Combat Logic
   - Simple damage calculations
   - Clear health tracking
   - Straightforward capture mechanics

3. Error Prevention
   - Validate state before updates
   - Clear error logging
   - Simple recovery paths

## Battle Flow
### Pre-Battle Phase (3 seconds)
- Battalion placement validation
- Initial state setup
- Network line assignments
- Resource allocation
- Display countdown overlay
- Show deployment zones
- Animate network nodes and connection lines

### Active Battle Phase (20 seconds)
- Battle Timer
  - Simple 20-second countdown display
  - Located at screen top
  - No intermediate warnings
  - Continuous countdown until completion
- Turn-based combat system
- Clear action sequence
- State updates after each action
- Real-time feedback

### Results Phase
- Victory condition checking
- Score calculation
- Battle summary generation
- State cleanup

## Victory Conditions
### Scoring System
- Mark-Based Point Values
  - Mark 1: 1 point per bot
  - Mark 2: 2 points per bot
  - Mark 3: 4 points per bot
  - Mark 4: 8 points per bot
- Bot type does not affect point value
- Lower total = better performance

### Victory Determination
- Track losses for both sides
- Calculate total loss points
- Determine winner based on:
  1. Node control majority
  2. Lower loss points
  3. Time-based tiebreaker

## Performance Standards
1. State Updates
   - Atomic operations
   - Direct state transitions
   - Clear update patterns
   - Performance monitoring

2. Error Handling
   - Follow backend error standards
   - Maintain clear error boundaries
   - Log errors consistently
   - Recover gracefully from failures

Remember: Changes must directly support these core mechanics and maintain system integrity. 